1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. c3 f5 4. d4 fxe4 5. Nxe5 Nf6 6. Bg5 Be7 7. Bc4 d5 8. Bb5 Bd7 9. Bxc6 Bxc6 10. Nd2 O-O 11. O-O Nd7 {(Black has gained the initiative)} 12. Nxc6 bxc6 13. Bxe7 {(White offered a draw with this move)} Qxe7 $15 14. Qe2 Rae8 15. f3 e3 16. Nb3 c5 17. dxc5 Nxc5 18. Nd4 Na4 19. Qb5 Nb6 20. Rae1 Qd6 21. Qd3 Nc4 22. Re2 c5 23. Nf5 Qe5 24. Ng3 Nb6 25. Rd1 Rf4 26. Rde1 d4 27. Ne4 Rd8 $4 (27... Rxe4 $1 28. fxe4 Qxe4 {and now White would have to find} 29. Rd2 $1 {to stay in the game.}) 28. cxd4 cxd4 29. Rxe3 $1 Qa5 $2 ({Black should have taken his chances with} 29... dxe3 $1 30. Qxd8+ Rf8 31. Qd3 Qxb2 32. a3 {, etc.}) 30. R3e2 Qxa2 $2 (30... Rd5 31. Qd2 {and White should win with the extra pawn}) 31. Ng5 $1 {Source: John Saunders} 1-0

